From 5a4e680b29618c06ac993bad1db0620dbf0688ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:41:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 142/149] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: Flatten the USB controller
 nodes

Describe both DWC3 controllers with the flattened qcom,snps-dwc3
binding, as SM8450 and later already are, so that dwc3-qcom drives them
instead of dwc3-qcom-legacy. The glue and the core become one node: the
core's interrupt comes first ("dwc_usb3"), the register range covers the
core and QSCRATCH, and the core properties and the port graph move up
from the removed child nodes. Boards that set the child's dr_mode, role
switch or pinctrl now set them on the controller node; the endpoint
labels stay the same.

Only the flattened driver is told about role changes: dwc3 calls the
glue's pre_set_role and pre_run_stop hooks, and dwc3-qcom clears the
QSCRATCH VBUS override when the role leaves "device" and sets it again
when it comes back. With the legacy layout the override is set once at
probe and never cleared, so in device mode the controller never sees a
session end when the cable is pulled.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
